<%# THIS FILE IS WHITESPACE-SENSITIVE — do not reformat on save.

    The LANDGRAB wordmark relies on there being ZERO whitespace
    between the letter <span>s. `.landgrab-wordmark-text` uses
    inline layout (not flex), so any inter-tag whitespace becomes
    a visible gap between letters — the HEEx formatter helpfully
    adds that whitespace, so this element lives in its own file so
    the parent page can be safely reformatted.

    Each letter sits in a static-position "slot" that owns hover
    detection; the inner span is what visually drops out. The slot
    stays put, so once the cursor enters, the letter keeps falling
    even if the pointer doesn't chase it. `aria-label` on the
    enclosing `.landgrab-wordmark` carries the readable name;
    these inner spans are decorative. %>
<span class="landgrab-wordmark-text" aria-hidden="true"><%= for letter <- String.graphemes("LANDGRAB") do %><span class="landgrab-letter-slot"><span class="landgrab-letter"><%= letter %></span></span><% end %></span>
